  "body": "Found during the work on #3258 (review of PR #3302, comment 7075899808). PR #3302 makes the gate name a signal that kills a test binary. It cannot show these two faults, because the runner itself stopped and the gate wrote no summary.\n\n1. Run 44982953354 (c05291a8b), runner skull: the gate job stayed in the step \"Batch gate tier\" for 63 minutes (a normal run takes about 22). The coordinator cancelled it. No log is available.\n2. Run 44995766211 attempt 1 (d911f4553), runner uma, 06:53Z to 07:07Z: the annotation says \"self-hosted runner lost communication with the server\". The job has no log.\n\nExpected: find the cause on the runner hosts (service logs of the runner, memory, disk, network at those times). Add a job-level timeout or a heartbeat so that a hung gate ends with a visible reason. Name the runner in the rolling \"main is red\" issue for a runner stop.\n",
